1
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Maria is a history, drama, music film directed by Pablo Larraín.

2
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Maria Callas, the world's greatest opera singer, lives the last days of her
life in 1970s Paris, as she confronts her identity and life.

3
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Maria Callas, played by Angelina Jolie.

4
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Ferruccio, played by Pierfrancesco Favino.

5
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Bruna, played by Alba Rohrwacher.

6
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Aristotle Onassis, played by Haluk Bilginer.

7
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:30,000
Mandrax, played by Kodi Smit-McPhee.

8
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:42,000
Jeffrey Tate, played by Stephen Ashfield.

9
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Maria is a 2024 biographical psychological drama film directed
by Pablo Larraín and written by Steven Knight.

10
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
It is an international co-production between Italy,
Chile, Germany and the United States.

11
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:18,000
The film stars Angelina Jolie as opera singer Maria Callas, and follows the week
before her death in 1977 Paris, as she reflects on her life and career.

12
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
It also stars Pierfrancesco Favino, Alba Rohrwacher, Haluk Bilginer, Stephen
Ashfield, Valeria Golino, and Kodi Smit-McPhee in supporting roles.

13
01:20:36,000 --> 01:20:42,000
It is the third film in Larraín's trilogy of iconic 20th-century
women, following Jackie (2016), and Spencer (2021).

14
01:26:48,000 --> 01:26:54,000
The film premiered at the 81st Venice International Film Festival on August 29, 2024, where it competed for the Golden
Lion and received generally positive reviews from critics, who singled out Jolie's performance for praise.

15
01:33:00,000 --> 01:33:06,000
It was released in select theaters in the United States on November
27, 2024, before streaming on Netflix on December 11.

16
01:39:12,000 --> 01:39:18,000
It was theatrically released in Italy by 01 Distribution on January 1, 2025,
before its release in Germany by StudioCanal on February 6.

17
01:45:24,000 --> 01:45:30,000
The film earned a nomination for Best Cinematography at the 97th Academy Awards, while Jolie was
nominated for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama at the 82nd Golden Globe Awards.

18
01:51:36,000 --> 01:51:42,000
The film explores themes of opera, paris, france, 1970s, surrealism, biography.

19
01:57:48,000 --> 01:57:54,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
